From 68d58bf98e43a18148bd70876b81ee7f8f46ac96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:45:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(multiaxis): the Rotary Flow multi-band and
 single-helix kernel

The picked guide chains read as ONE ordered set (#2829), in a new
rotary_flow_set module of the motion crate:

- three or more ordered chains machine one band per adjacent pair,
  and the SHARED boundary chain is cut once - band k > 0 starts at
  its first interior pass;
- a single chain machines the full revolution: the kernel morphs it
  to its own next lap (th + TAU in the unwrap's own reading), the
  developed band is exactly one revolution wide, and the lap's
  closing pass is dropped because the lap's two edges are one world
  curve;
- a chain wound against its pair is walked backwards (the feature
  layer reads a chain's direction from the mesh, never from the
  pick) - superseding #2824's opposite-sense refusal, said in the
  notes;
- chains that meet or cross are refused by name at the shared spot
  (the exact segment-pair law), and bands that double back through
  the chain before them are refused as a set out of band order.

The app wiring needed no change: the picks already ride the chains
into the kernel. App-level pins on the turned bar: three ring chains
cut two bands with the boundary once; one meridian chain machines
the full revolution (19 passes, one landing per azimuth); the
meridian-plus-ring set refuses at the shared corner.

Fixes #2829
